\section{PORTO-package}
\markboth{PORTO-package}{PORTO-package}
\index{PORTO-package}
\field{Description}
PORTO implements ordinal preferences on the virtual contributions of DEA and BoD indicators. The four public functions distinguish radial from directional models and rankings without ties from those with ties. All functions solve one linear program for each DMU, using every supplied observation as a reference unit. Use the original values in the directional model, with undesirable indicators supplied separately.
\field{Installation}
After creating a GitHub repository, upload the contents of the PORTO source folder into its root (including DESCRIPTION and NAMESPACE). Replace the username and repository with your actual GitHub address.
\begin{verbatim}
install.packages("remotes")
remotes::install_github("usuario/PORTO")
library(PORTO)
help(package = "PORTO")
?dea.order
?dir.dea.order.ties
\end{verbatim}
For a local source installation, use \texttt{remotes::install\_local("path/to/PORTO")} or \texttt{R CMD INSTALL PORTO}. To rebuild the native R manual and check the package, run these commands from the parent folder:
\begin{verbatim}
